Two bugs in Infusion Studio v4:

BUG 1 — In src/app/(dashboard)/recipes/page.tsx, the rateRecipe function calls:
setDetailRecipe({ ...recipe, rating });
But this uses the old recipe object from closure, not the freshly-saved API response. Replace with:
const rateRecipe = async (recipe: RecipeWithBlend, rating: number) => {
  const res = await fetch(`/api/recipes/${recipe.id}`, {
    method: 'PATCH',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ rating }),
  });
  if (!res.ok) { toast('Failed to save rating'); return; }
  const updated = await res.json();
  setDetailRecipe(updated);
  fetchRecipes();
};

BUG 2 — In src/app/(dashboard)/settings/page.tsx, if a user submits an empty socialHandle the API returns 400 with { error: 'Handle must be at least 3 characters' } but no toast shows. Fix the onSubmit function:
const res = await fetch('/api/profile', { method: 'PUT', ... });
if (!res.ok) {
  const err = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
  toast(err.error ?? 'Failed to save settings');
  return;
}

Also update src/app/api/profile/route.ts PUT handler: if socialHandle is an empty string, set data.socialHandle = null instead of returning 400. This allows users to clear their handle.

